WEBVTT

00:00.330 --> 00:03.100
- [Instructor] We're told a
monkey is swinging from a tree.

00:03.100 --> 00:08.100
On the first swing, she passes
through an arc of 24 meters.

00:08.180 --> 00:10.930
With each swing, she passes through an arc

00:10.930 --> 00:14.120
1/2 the length of the previous swing.

00:14.120 --> 00:15.050
So what's going on here?

00:15.050 --> 00:16.530
Let's say this is the top of the rope

00:16.530 --> 00:18.800
or the vine that the
monkey is swinging from.

00:18.800 --> 00:21.140
And so on that first swing,

00:21.140 --> 00:22.870
I like to draw a little monkey here,

00:22.870 --> 00:25.690
so this is my little monkey.

00:25.690 --> 00:30.690
So on the first swing, the
monkey will go 24 meters.

00:30.740 --> 00:33.250
Might do something like this.

00:33.250 --> 00:35.030
Then that arc is 24 meters,

00:35.030 --> 00:36.700
and then on the second swing,

00:36.700 --> 00:38.810
it would be, she'd swing back at an arc

00:38.810 --> 00:41.810
half the length of the previous swing.

00:41.810 --> 00:43.650
So then she would come back

00:43.650 --> 00:45.610
and then it would be half the length,

00:45.610 --> 00:47.510
and so maybe swing back over here.

00:47.510 --> 00:49.650
And then on the next, so that'd be 12,

00:49.650 --> 00:53.370
and then on the next swing,
she would swing half of that,

00:53.370 --> 00:55.350
which would be six meters.

00:55.350 --> 00:56.980
And so she might swing like this,

00:56.980 --> 00:57.840
and that makes sense.

00:57.840 --> 01:00.630
That's consistent with our
experiences swinging from trees,

01:00.630 --> 01:02.410
for those of us who have done that.

01:02.410 --> 01:04.740
(laughs) So let's look
at the first choice.

01:04.740 --> 01:06.840
Which expression gives the total length

01:06.840 --> 01:10.980
the monkey swings in her first n swings?

01:10.980 --> 01:12.640
So pause the video and
see if you can do that,

01:12.640 --> 01:14.350
and you can express it as,

01:14.350 --> 01:15.710
actually express it two ways,

01:15.710 --> 01:18.440
express it as a geometric series,

01:18.440 --> 01:22.210
but also express it as the
sum of a geometric series

01:22.210 --> 01:23.773
if it were actually evaluated.

01:25.130 --> 01:26.790
So let's do this together.

01:26.790 --> 01:29.390
So we already said on the first swing,

01:29.390 --> 01:33.210
the monkey goes 24 meters.

01:33.210 --> 01:35.000
Now on the second swing,
and I gave you a hint

01:35.000 --> 01:38.360
when I said to express
it as a geometric series,

01:38.360 --> 01:39.980
she swings half that.

01:39.980 --> 01:41.750
Now I could just write a 12 here,

01:41.750 --> 01:43.090
but the half is interesting.

01:43.090 --> 01:44.840
Because that's going to be my common ratio

01:44.840 --> 01:46.280
for my geometric series.

01:46.280 --> 01:48.290
Every successive swing,

01:48.290 --> 01:51.410
the arc length is half the
arc length of the last swing.

01:51.410 --> 01:56.140
So it's going to be 24 times 1/2

01:56.140 --> 01:58.580
and then on the next
swing, it's going to be 24,

01:58.580 --> 01:59.670
it's going to be half of this.

01:59.670 --> 02:02.270
So it's going to be 24
times 1/2 times 1/2.

02:02.270 --> 02:06.400
So that's 24 times 1/2
to the second power.

02:06.400 --> 02:09.030
And so this would be
the first three swings.

02:09.030 --> 02:12.350
Notice that the exponent here,
we got to the second power.

02:12.350 --> 02:14.310
So the first n swings,

02:14.310 --> 02:16.180
we are going to get to

02:16.180 --> 02:19.680
24 times 1/2, not to the nth power,

02:19.680 --> 02:22.170
but to the n minus one power.

02:22.170 --> 02:23.850
Notice, after two swings, we only get

02:23.850 --> 02:25.940
to 24 times 1/2 to the first power.

02:25.940 --> 02:27.580
After three swings, to the second power.

02:27.580 --> 02:31.250
So after n swings, to
the n minus one power.

02:31.250 --> 02:33.830
Now, as I said, we don't wanna
just have this expression.

02:33.830 --> 02:36.670
We actually wanna know,
how do we evaluate this?

02:36.670 --> 02:38.410
And the way we evaluate this

02:38.410 --> 02:40.530
is we look at the formula,
which we've explained

02:40.530 --> 02:42.300
and we've proven in other videos,

02:42.300 --> 02:45.970
the formula for a finite geometric series.

02:45.970 --> 02:49.140
So that tells us, and I'll
just write it over here,

02:49.140 --> 02:52.180
the sum of first

02:54.735 --> 02:55.818
n terms is a,

02:59.025 --> 03:00.690
where a is the first term.

03:00.690 --> 03:03.520
So that's going to be
our 24 in this situation.

03:03.520 --> 03:06.590
It's a minus a

03:06.590 --> 03:08.330
times our common ratio,

03:08.330 --> 03:11.133
I already said that our
common ratio is 1/2,

03:12.350 --> 03:15.420
to the nth power.

03:15.420 --> 03:17.420
So one way I like to remember it is,

03:17.420 --> 03:20.810
it is our first term minus the first term

03:20.810 --> 03:22.060
that we didn't include,

03:22.060 --> 03:25.950
or minus what would've been
the term right after this.

03:25.950 --> 03:29.690
All of that over one
minus our common ratio.

03:29.690 --> 03:32.410
And there's other ways that
you might've seen this written.

03:32.410 --> 03:33.890
You could factor an a out,

03:33.890 --> 03:35.400
and you might have seen
something like this:

03:35.400 --> 03:38.660
a times one minus r to the n,

03:38.660 --> 03:42.240
all of that over one minus
r, these two are equivalent.

03:42.240 --> 03:44.200
But now let's use this.

03:44.200 --> 03:46.470
So this is going to be equal to,

03:46.470 --> 03:49.370
actually I'll use this
second form right over here.

03:49.370 --> 03:51.890
So our first term a is 24.

03:51.890 --> 03:53.740
So we're going to have 24

03:53.740 --> 03:57.820
times one minus our common
ratio, which is 1/2,

03:57.820 --> 04:00.750
to the nth power, well we're talking about

04:00.750 --> 04:03.390
the first n swing, so I'm
just going to leave an n

04:03.390 --> 04:04.590
right over there.

04:04.590 --> 04:09.510
All of that over one
minus our common ratio,

04:09.510 --> 04:11.970
one minus 1/2.

04:11.970 --> 04:13.380
So we could leave it like that

04:13.380 --> 04:16.000
or we could simplify it
a little bit if we like.

04:16.000 --> 04:19.343
One minus 1/2 is equal to 1/2,

04:20.250 --> 04:23.210
24 divided by 1/2 is equal to 48,

04:23.210 --> 04:24.900
so if you wanted to, you could simplify it

04:24.900 --> 04:26.750
to 48 times one minus 1/2

04:28.030 --> 04:30.230
to the nth power.

04:30.230 --> 04:32.710
So either of these would be legitimate.

04:32.710 --> 04:34.220
Now the second part, they say,

04:34.220 --> 04:36.390
what is the total distance
the monkey has traveled

04:36.390 --> 04:40.480
when she completes her 25th swing?

04:40.480 --> 04:42.800
And they say, round your final
answer to the nearest meter.

04:42.800 --> 04:46.070
So pause this video and see
if you can work that out.

04:46.070 --> 04:49.610
All right, well, we can just
use this expression here.

04:49.610 --> 04:53.520
And we know that we are
completing our 25th swing.

04:53.520 --> 04:57.390
So n is 25, and so we'll
just put a 25 there.

04:57.390 --> 05:00.450
So that's going to be
48 times one minus 1/2

05:01.480 --> 05:04.730
to the 25th power.

05:04.730 --> 05:07.650
Now this is going to
be a very, very small,

05:07.650 --> 05:08.770
very, very small number.

05:08.770 --> 05:10.850
So it's actually going to be pretty close

05:10.850 --> 05:14.980
to 48 meters, but let's
see what this is equal to.

05:14.980 --> 05:17.530
And we're going to round
to the nearest meter.

05:17.530 --> 05:19.450
All right, so let's
get our calculator out.

05:19.450 --> 05:21.920
And so let's just evaluate 1/2,

05:21.920 --> 05:23.850
I'll just write that as 0.5

05:23.850 --> 05:26.870
to the 25th power,

05:26.870 --> 05:30.000
which, as we said, as we
predicted, is a very small number.

05:30.000 --> 05:31.590
And then we're going to
subtract that from one,

05:31.590 --> 05:34.670
so I'll just put a negative
and then I'll add one to it.

05:34.670 --> 05:37.510
And so that is very close to one.

05:37.510 --> 05:39.640
And so my prediction is holding true.

05:39.640 --> 05:42.680
So if I multiply that times 48,

05:42.680 --> 05:44.150
well, if we round to the nearest meter,

05:44.150 --> 05:45.950
we get back to 48 meters.

05:45.950 --> 05:49.400
So this is going to be 48 meters.

05:49.400 --> 05:50.453
And we're done.
